details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. Composition: two simple, round, matte-white ceramic bowls are centered on a weathered, aged oak wooden table, arranged for a home-cooked meal for two. The primary bowl in the foreground is in sharp focus, while the second bowl sits slightly behind and blurred to establish depth. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead at 40 degrees, allowing a clear view into both bowls. Lighting: soft, natural side light from a window to the left, creating gentle highlights on the chowder's surface and subtle, soft shadows. The chowder has a creamy, opaque, off-white base from the milk and mashed potatoes, punctuated by bright yellow kernels of sweet corn, soft-edged cubes of red potato skin, and chunks of tender, pink flaked salmon. The surface features a delicate dusting of reddish smoked paprika and a generous sprinkling of freshly chopped vibrant green chives. Styling: a rumpled, neutral linen napkin is tucked partially under the base of the front bowl, and a rustic wooden spoon rests casually on the table surface next to it. Nearby, a few stray bits of chopped chives and a single, small piece of flaked salmon lie on the wood, suggesting a natural, lived-in cooking process. Realism: photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a warm, cozy kitchen atmosphere with golden-hour color temperature. Includes realistic, slight imperfections: a tiny splash of broth on the rim of the bowl and uneven texture where the potatoes were mashed. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial cookbook photography."
  }
]
